        2197,
        3366
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "(4) Any employee may present his own grievance through the first four steps of the grievance procedure either personally or through an appropriate representative or through an organization of which he is a member, provided, that where an employee organization has been certified as the exclusive bargaining agent for the employee unit, a grievance may be presented and processed either by such certified employee organization or by the individual employee, but not through any other employee organization.",
